STEP 11 — EPIC 2: Authentication & Authorization

What was built:
- Staff login with JWT (short-lived access token + long-lived refresh token).
  Refresh tokens are stored (as a SHA-256 hash) in `refresh_tokens`, so
  logging out revokes them for real.
- Passwords are hashed with bcrypt (passlib) before they are stored.
- Role-based access: inspektor, drejtor, admin. Citizens have no account.
- NO self-registration. Staff accounts are created only by an admin
  (POST /admin/users, "Përdoruesit & rolet" page) or by the seed script.
- Admin user management: list, create, edit, deactivate / reactivate.
- Frontend: landing page, split-screen login, welcome message after login
  ("Mirë se erdhe, {emri}! Roli juaj është {roli}."), placeholder dashboard
  per role, admin "Përdoruesit & rolet" page.
- The coat of arms (frontend/public/stema.svg) is the logo everywhere:
  landing, login, app sidebar, citizen page and browser tab icon.
- No new migration was needed: `perdoruesit` and `refresh_tokens` already
  exist from migration 0001 ("alembic check" is still clean).

