   Covered: /auth/register does not exist, login (correct / wrong password /
   inactive user), refresh, logout (revoked token can't refresh), /auth/me
   (valid / missing / expired / forged / refresh-token-as-access), role
   routes (allowed vs 403), admin create (every role, bcrypt hash stored,
   sector, duplicate email, short password) / edit / deactivate.

2. Live end-to-end check (backend + frontend running, seed users created):
       backend\venv\Scripts\python.exe test\e2e_auth_flow.py
   If Vite runs on 5174, first:  $env:E2E_FRONTEND = "http://localhost:5174"
   Real HTTP against the real database: admin creates an inspektor -> login
   -> protected route -> refresh -> logout -> admin user management, plus
   CORS, "no /auth/register", and the frontend pages. It deletes the users
   it creates.

3. Frontend checks (from inside frontend/):
       npm run lint
       npm run build

4. By hand: open the frontend, log in with a seed account above, and you
   land on that role's dashboard. Its "Qasja në API" card shows LEJUAR when
   the protected route accepted you.

