-------------------------------------------------------------------------
DECISIONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
- No registration at all: there is no register page and no /auth/register.
  Where a "create account" link would be, the landing and login pages say
  "Llogaritë krijohen nga administratori i inspektoratit."
- Design: the landing and login pages follow the reference screenshots
  (dark hero, split-screen login, blue accent #2563EB). The staff app
  screens follow the design specification PDF (teal accent #0D9488).
- Welcome message: shown once on the dashboard right after a login; it does
  not come back on reload or when returning to the dashboard.
- Logo: frontend/public/stema.svg is the coat of arms of the Republic of
  Kosovo (from the provided file). To use the Vushtrri municipal crest
  instead, replace that one file.
- Sector: optional, read from `kategorite` (top-level rows). The table is
  empty until categories are seeded, so the dropdown shows
  "Nuk ka sektorë ende".
- Tokens: access 15 min, refresh 7 days (ACCESS_TOKEN_MINUTES,
  REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS in backend/.env). /auth/refresh returns a new access
  token and keeps the same refresh token (no rotation).
- Token storage in the browser: access token only in memory; refresh token
  in localStorage so a page reload keeps you logged in. The API client
  refreshes automatically on a 401 and logs out if that fails.
- Deactivated users cannot log in, refresh, or use an old access token, and
  all their refresh tokens are revoked. An admin cannot deactivate or demote
  their own account (so the system never loses its admin by accident).
- Users are never deleted, only deactivated.
- passlib: the original passlib 1.7.4 is unmaintained and breaks with
  bcrypt 5, so the maintained drop-in fork "libpass" is installed (the code
  still does "from passlib.context import CryptContext"). Passwords must be
  8–72 bytes (bcrypt's limit).
- JWT library: PyJWT. JWT_SECRET is in backend/.env (generated, never
  committed). The app refuses to start without it.
- Starlette's test client now wants "httpx2" instead of "httpx", so httpx2
  is installed.
- New backend settings in .env / .env.example: JWT_SECRET,
  ACCESS_TOKEN_MINUTES, REFRESH_TOKEN_DAYS, FRONTEND_ORIGIN
  (comma-separated list of allowed frontend addresses).
